From 7e19ad9d03e9b4a9d480454f7db5c98cb9c7dc01 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jernej Skrabec <jernej.skrabec@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Mar 2026 16:52:18 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 216/273] drm/sun4i: mixer: Configure YUV scanline limits per
 channel

Display Engine channels can have different YUV scaler line-buffer
limits. Replace the single mixer-wide limit with one value per VI
channel and use the matching value during plane checks.

The per-channel array lives in struct sun8i_layer_cfg, so MAX_CHANNELS
has to move from the planes header into the mixer header. Grow it to 9
while at it, to cover the H616 layout of three VI channels plus UI
channels at physical indexes 6 to 8.

Signed-off-by: Jernej Skrabec <jernej.skrabec@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun50i_planes.c  |  2 +-
 drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun50i_planes.h  |  1 -
 drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun8i_mixer.c    | 22 +++++++++++-----------
 drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun8i_mixer.h    |  6 ++++--
 drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun8i_vi_layer.c |  5 ++++-
 5 files changed, 20 insertions(+), 16 deletions(-)

